-- title:
--   Residual eigenvalues cut out the corner in F ⊗_𝒪 H
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $H$ be a finite free $\mathcal O$-module. Let $D$ be a `HeckeData`, i.e. a type $D.\mathrm{Gen}$ of generators, a family of pairwise commuting $\mathcal O$-endomorphisms $D.\mathrm{op}(g)$ of $H$, and prescribed residual values $D.\bar\theta(g) \in k$; write $\mathbb T = D.\mathrm{opSubalgebra}$ for the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H)$ generated by the $D.\mathrm{op}(g)$. Let $Sp$ be an `IdempotentSplitting` of $\mathbb T$: a number $n$, idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ forming a complete orthogonal family, maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb T$, with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j$ exactly when $i \neq j$. Fix $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0} D.\mathrm{op}(g) e_{i_0}) = D.\bar\theta(g)$ for all $g$. Let $F$ be a field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\mathcal O \to F$ injective. Call $x \in F$ residually $c \in k$ if there is a monic $R \in \mathcal O[X]$ with $R(x) = 0$ whose reduction to $k[X]$ is $(X - c)^{\deg R}$. For $a : D.\mathrm{Gen} \to F$ put $V_a = \bigcap_g$ (maximal generalised eigenspace of $D.\mathrm{op}(g) \otimes 1$ on $F \otimes_{\mathcal O} H$ for the eigenvalue $a(g)$), and let $\mathrm{Cor}$ be the image in $F \otimes_{\mathcal O} H$ of the base change of the inclusion of the corner submodule $e_{i_0} H = \mathrm{range}(e_{i_0} \bullet \mathrm{id})$, viewed $\mathcal O$-linearly. Then: (1) if $a(g)$ is residually $D.\bar\theta(g)$ for every $g$, then $V_a \le \mathrm{Cor}$; (2) if $a(g)$ fails to be residually $D.\bar\theta(g)$ for some $g$, then $V_a \sqcap \mathrm{Cor} = \bot$; (3) if $F$ is algebraically closed, then $\mathrm{Cor}$ equals the supremum of the $V_a$ over all tuples $a$ with $a(g)$ residually $D.\bar\theta(g)$ for every $g$.
--
--   This identifies the $\mathfrak m$-part $e_{i_0}H$ of the Hecke module, after base change to a field $F$ containing $\mathcal O$, purely by conditions on the simultaneous generalised eigenvalues of the operators $D.\mathrm{op}(g)$: a tuple contributes precisely when each of its eigenvalues is residually the prescribed value $D.\bar\theta(g)$. It is used in the multiplicity computation for corner realisations, namely in [`CohCarrier.finrank_range_baseChange_cornerSubmodule_inf_iInf_eigenspace_heckeTL_eq_two_mul_prod_sum_rootMultiplicity`](thm.html#CohCarrier.finrank_range_baseChange_cornerSubmodule_inf_iInf_eigenspace_heckeTL_eq_two_mul_prod_sum_rootMultiplicity) and in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_algebraicClosure_residual_isRoot_of_linearEquiv_cornerSubmodule`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_algebraicClosure_residual_isRoot_of_linearEquiv_cornerSubmodule).
